*.pdf binary

# Every text file in this repository's git history is already stored with
# LF line endings (verified via `git cat-file -p` against committed blobs).
# Without this rule, a contributor whose local `core.autocrlf` is `true`
# (the Git for Windows default) gets those same LF blobs converted to CRLF
# on checkout. That conversion is invisible for most source files, but it
# silently breaks:
#   - the `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang line on `.github/scripts/*.mjs`
#     scripts, which Vite/Vitest's SSR module transform cannot parse when
#     it is CRLF-terminated (plain `node` tolerates it fine, which is why
#     this class of failure is invisible outside the test runner);
#   - `\n`-anchored regexes in `.test.ts` files that parse checked-out
#     `.yml`/`.mjs` content (e.g. `src/__tests__/unit/
#     supabasePreviewValidateWorkflow.test.ts` matching workflow-job
#     boundaries in `.github/workflows/*.yml`).
# Forcing LF on checkout, regardless of any individual contributor's local
# `core.autocrlf`, removes the whole class of failure at its source instead
# of working around it file-by-file. Git's own text/binary heuristic
# (`text=auto`) still leaves genuinely binary assets alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
